 ```
 
+A show is designed against the catalog and fired from the magazine, and those
+are never the same list. Give any show command the magazine book and the
+compiler draws every cue out of it, substitutes a shell of the same calibre
+where the shelf is short, writes the lot each cue came from onto the cue sheet,
+and refuses the show when nothing on the shelf will do.
+
+```
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig \
+  --magazine magazine.csv --pull vn2405,vn2413
+```
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
